        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-9> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py, docs/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png, datasets/levin_youtube_channel/levin_youtube_catalog.json, morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean, morphoeval/runs/levin_youtube_channel_math_summary.json implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Multicellular bioelectric collectives, non-neural Gene Regulatory Networks (GRNs), and driven active-matter morphospaces specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 93.8/100, audit 2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a2201fd3/datasets/levin_youtube_channel/levin_youtube_catalog.json>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a2201fd3/docs/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a2201fd3/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a2201fd3/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a2201fd3/morphoeval/runs/levin_youtube_channel_math_summary.json> ;
    schema:about "Multicellular bioelectric collectives, non-neural Gene Regulatory Networks (GRNs), and driven active-matter morphospaces" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Separates proven mathematical invariants of driven Markov/GRN/bioelectric networks from philosophical claims of disembodied mind-stuff ingressing outside physical law",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Complete SHA-256-locked catalog of all 374 videos on @drmichaellevin across 8 categories, paired with executable Python verification and 6 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems (0 sorry) in MathOfBiology.lean and Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean",
        "reported_in_source: Across 374 videos (333.05 hours, 2,508,589 views) on @drmichaellevin, Levin and guest speakers (Pavel Chvykov, Marc Finzi, Andrew Wilson, Richard Watson, Federico Pigozzi, Josh Bongard, Cristi Stoica, Tom Froese, Lakshwin Shreesha, Alexandre Morozov, Buck Trible, Karl Friston, and Joel Dietz) present formal models of TAME cognitive light cones, low-rattling pattern selection, polycomputing, GRN natural induction, epiplexity, and multicellular game theory",
        "transfer_boundary: Demonstrates that Chvykov's Low-Rattling law (P_ss(x) ~ r_exit(x)^(-gamma)), Finzi-Wilson Epiplexity (L_F = E_F + H_F), Bongard-Levin Polycomputing, and Watson-Pigozzi Hebbian GRN conditioning provide exact dynamical and statistical-mechanics mechanisms (P_structural) for apparent 'Platonic' free lunches without requiring non-physical dualist intervention (P_dualist)" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a2201fd3/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a2201fd3/docs/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a2201fd3/datasets/levin_youtube_channel/levin_youtube_catalog.json, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a2201fd3/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a2201fd3/morphoeval/runs/levin_youtube_channel_math_summary.json; output: media/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png; organism: Multicellular bioelectric collectives, non-neural Gene Regulatory Networks (GRNs), and driven active-matter morphospaces; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/a2201fd3; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Across 374 videos (333.05 hours, 2,508,589 views) on @drmichaellevin, Levin and guest speakers (Pavel Chvykov, Marc Finzi, Andrew Wilson, Richard Watson, Federico Pigozzi, Josh Bongard, Cristi Stoica, Tom Froese, Lakshwin Shreesha, Alexandre Morozov, Buck Trible, Karl Friston, and Joel Dietz) present formal models of TAME cognitive light cones, low-rattling pattern selection, polycomputing, GRN natural induction, epiplexity, and multicellular game theory; reconstructed_in_script: Complete SHA-256-locked catalog of all 374 videos on @drmichaellevin across 8 categories, paired with executable Python verification and 6 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems (0 sorry) in MathOfBiology.lean and Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean; transfer_boundary: Demonstrates that Chvykov's Low-Rattling law (P_ss(x) ~ r_exit(x)^(-gamma)), Finzi-Wilson Epiplexity (L_F = E_F + H_F), Bongard-Levin Polycomputing, and Watson-Pigozzi Hebbian GRN conditioning provide exact dynamical and statistical-mechanics mechanisms (P_structural) for apparent 'Platonic' free lunches without requiring non-physical dualist intervention (P_dualist); does_not_claim: Separates proven mathematical invariants of driven Markov/GRN/bioelectric networks from philosophical claims of disembodied mind-stuff ingressing outside physical law]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-025-08411-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abc6182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnsys.2022.768201>,
